# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Settings template.
#  • Local dev: copy this file to ".env" and fill in values.
#  • Hugging Face: set these under Space → Settings → "Variables and secrets"
#    (use "secret" for keys/DB URL, "variable" for the rest).
# Everything here is optional — with nothing set, the app runs on ephemeral
# SQLite with LLM explanations disabled.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Persistent database. Paste your Neon/Supabase/Railway Postgres URL here.
# Accepts the provider's raw URL (sslmode/channel_binding params are handled).
# If unreachable at startup, the app falls back to in-memory storage for the session.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@ep-xxx.region.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require

# LLM provider for root-cause explanations.
# Groq is used automatically when GROQ_API_KEY is set (free + fast); else OpenRouter.
# GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# GROQ_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Built-in synthetic traffic generator (live demo). Set false to ingest only external data.
# ENABLE_SYNTHETIC=true
# SYNTHETIC_DELAY=2.0
